part gen_1
  tally 2
  law
  note "GEN-1 · Business days and public holidays. holidays is the calendar next_business and prev_business read (L §4.2): one row per year, the fixed days of GEN-1 .2 plus that year's Spring Day from its notice (HOL-SPRING-<yyyy>)."
  note "A year's row sits in the version of its Spring Day notice, known on the notice's publication day: a dates value is one list, so the fixed days, settled since 2017-06-01 (2024-06-18 for 23 June), can't be known before the notice that completes the list (observation O:A-3). A year with no notice has no row (GEN-1 .3)."

source gen_1 "General Provisions Act, GEN-1 Business days and public holidays (tmp/cases/law/acts.md)"

input holidays: calendar question "Which days of this year are public holidays (GEN-1 .2, and the Spring Day notice of GEN-1 .3)?"

